.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 1.18
.\"
.TH "StreamToken" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
StreamToken \- Generate position information for a data stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]StreamToken()\f[]
.PP
\f[B]StreamToken(<token>)\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
StreamToken
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to generate a token contains position information for a
data stream.
It allows for reading the data stream from the latest position, or reading from
a specified position.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
token (\f[I]string, optional\f[])
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
The position information string indicating from where to start reading the data stream.
\f[]
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it returns the generated StreamToken
object.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens, use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v7.2.2 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Generate a token for reading the data stream from the latest position:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> var token = new StreamToken()
\f[]
.fi
.PP
Generate a token for reading the data stream from a specified position:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> var token = StreamToken("00010000000003e800000000000000000000000000000ac80000000100000000")
\f[]
.fi
